parate build supports or set up Android SDK/NDK paths, or wait for Unity to download the iOS moniker. A fresh Unity install can barely build for your current PC without the proper platform modules. The “just hit build” magic stops the moment you try a platform you haven’t configured. That’s the dead giveaway that under the hood, entirely different toolchains are being summoned. So yes, from the developer’s chair, it *feels* like one simple step. But that’s because thousands of hours of engineering have already been spent to make the illusion hold. The actual compilation processes are as different as ever—the engine just hides the complexity so well that it seems like they don’t exist. That’s the genius of a modern engine, but it doesn’t invalidate the fact that compiling for a different platform is a fundamentally separate act.
